thread:
jess: FYI our CI started blowing up on the vitest edge runner after we switched SDK to ESM-only. stack: `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'prototype')` during a `vi.mock` of the client.

ana: probably an interop issue between the test runner expecting CJS-style exports and our ESM bundle. which node version in CI?

jess: GH actions uses node18-lts image for most jobs. local dev is node20 and it's fine.

lee: node18 + ESM can surface `exports is not defined` or weird prototype errors when a CJS dep gets transformed. Are you mocking a default or named export?

jess: mocking default. test: `vi.mock('my-sdk', () => ({ Client: MockClient }))` but package exports default `export default new Client()` in dist.

ana: two angles: change tests to match exports OR add a lightweight test shim that provides a CJS shape for older runners. For vitest you can also use `vi.stubModule` which respects ESM.

lee: sample vitest.config suggestion that fixed it for us:
```ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    environment: 'node',
    deps: {
      inline: [/msw/, /your-cjs-dep/]
    },
    esbuild: {
      platform: 'node',
      target: 'node18'
    }
  }
})
```
This forces deps to be transformed for ESM-compatible behavior and prevents automatic CJS bundling.

jess: tried deps.inline, helped some transitive errors but mock still not picked up in GH runner. stack points at `createRequire` flows inside a dep.

ana: alternative shim (works in both jest & vitest): add test/helpers/esm-to-cjs-shim.mjs that re-exports a cjs-compatible object:
```mjs
// test/helpers/esm-to-cjs-shim.mjs
import mod from '../../dist/index.mjs';
// create a simple wrapper with both default and named exports
export const defaultExport = mod.default ?? mod;
export const Client = (mod.default ?? mod).Client ?? (mod).Client;
export default defaultExport;
```
Then in tests `import sdk from 'test/helpers/esm-to-cjs-shim.mjs'` instead of `import 'my-sdk'` and use `vi.mock('./test/helpers/esm-to-cjs-shim.mjs', () => ({ default: { query: () => 'x' } }))`

lee: for jest specifically you may need to set `transformIgnorePatterns` to make jest transform ESM deps, or use `babel-jest`/`ts-jest` to handle imports. Also set `extensionsToTreatAsEsm: ['.ts', '.tsx', '.mjs']` in jest config when using node18 and ESM packages.

jess: typings also exploded: tests saw `Property 'createClient' does not exist on type 'typeof import("../dist")'`. Our types were `export =` style from older build.

ana: update d.ts to expose both shapes. Minimal root index.d.ts example:
```ts
declare class RedwoodClient { constructor(opts?: any); }
declare const _default: RedwoodClient;
export default _default;
export { RedwoodClient };
```
That covers `import sdk from 'my-sdk'` and `import { RedwoodClient } from 'my-sdk'` consumers.

build-bot: CI matrix note — running edge-runtime tests on node18 will continue to catch interop bugs. Recommend expanding test matrix to include node20 too.

lee: also consider adding an internal test entrypoint that builds a small CJS-only rollup for the test matrix only (not published). Example npm script: `build:test:cjs` that outputs `dist-test/index.cjs` used by tests in CI. Keeps publishing ESM-only but provides compatibility for runners.

jess: where should we put docs? the quickfixs are fragile and I'd like a canonical doc for devs.

ana: make a short DEVEX note with:
- vitest config snippet (deps.inline + esbuild platform node)
- example cjs-shim and esm-to-cjs-shim.mjs
- TS d.ts minimal pattern for default + named exports
- jest tips (extensionsToTreatAsEsm, transformIgnorePatterns)
- CI: add node20 to matrix or build-test:cjs step

jess: I'll open a PR with a `docs/devex/vitest-esm-interop.md` and include the shims + snippets. I'll also add a tiny integration test job that runs the edge runner against built artifacts in the PR pipeline.

qa-bot: run report: job 1760004321-edge-vitest failed 3/3 on node18. Artifacts: /artifacts/1760004321-vitest.log

lee: last tip: when writing mocks for ESM default, prefer `vi.mock('pkg', async () => { const real = await vi.importActual('pkg'); return { default: { ...real.default, doThing: () => 'x' } } })` — avoids accidental shape mismatches.

jess: awesome, thanks. I'll ping when PR is up for review.
